    "chapter_id": "6160253f32f74d11258840f1",
    "chapter_name": "Ellipse",
    "year": "2023",
    "shift": "shift_1"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> be the largest circle centred at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and inscribed in the ellipse&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;lies on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to ______</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "118",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Let any point on the ellipse be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0034_34c632f2087b.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 186px;\" /></p><p>Equation of normal of ellipse&nbsp;at&nbsp;any point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>sec</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>cosec</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>This normal is also the normal of the circle passing through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>sec</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> (Not possible)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;</p><p>So, point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>18</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>So, the largest radius of circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>320</mn></msqrt><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>64</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>So the equation of circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>64</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>This circle is passing through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, hence</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>64</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>59</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>118</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}